// spec: RT-009
//
// Val answers an Integer where the text is one, and a Double where it is not.
//
// ⚠️ This case used to pair Val with Max, because each was defensible alone --
// Val always yielding a Double, Max taking Integers only -- and together they
// left 'Max (Val (A), Val (B))' failing for EVERY input.  Max was removed in
// Generation 9 [RT-010]; what it proved about Val stands on its own.


WriteLn (Val ('42'));
WriteLn (Val ('42') is Integer);
WriteLn (Val ('-7'));
WriteLn (Val ('1.5'));
WriteLn (Val ('1.5') is Double);


